\id RUT
\h Ruth
\toc1 The Book of Ruth
\mt1 Ruth
\rem Fixture: the length lane. 20 verses, under min_verses 50, so the BOOK
\rem lane is i16::MIN and the project lane judges alone. 1:3 runs at a tenth
\rem of the length its source declares; the rest run within a few percent.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The sheep water’s fish vine of the sickle and the sickle beside the wall in the jar.
\v 2 The flame plough sickle’s of the harvest and the dye beside the ash in the flame.
\v 3 The seed of the field.
\v 4 The net rain’s of the spring and the river beside the orchard in the ash.
\v 5 The meadow lamp’s goat of the net and the thorn beside the net in the wick.
\v 6 The rope furrow’s of the thorn and the sheep beside the harvest in the olive.
\v 7 The fish basket jar’s of the jar and the spring beside the basket in the vine.
\v 8 The vine valley staff of the sickle and the yoke beside the ox in the river.
\v 9 The bread light of the wall and the meadow beside the field in the olive.
\v 10 The furrow jar road tower of the spring and the net beside the orchard in the fig.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 The wool sheep light of the linen and the staff beside the harvest in the thread.
\v 2 The pine flame of the stone and the olive beside the sheep in the linen.
\v 3 The goat ox of the dove and the thread beside the well in the dust.
\v 4 The fish brick of the meadow and the staff beside the field in the dye.
\v 5 The clay pine of the jar and the shore beside the harvest in the linen.
\v 6 The shore thorn of the sand and the water beside the flint in the seed.
\v 7 The cedar shore goat olive of the gate and the oil beside the jar in the brick.
\v 8 The linen lamp of the yoke and the orchard beside the stone in the plough.
\v 9 The ox beam staff of the ember and the sheep beside the rain in the thread.
\v 10 The staff hillside of the salt and the wick beside the tower in the pasture.
